abstract: "A finite algebra over epistemic states, implemented as a reproducible visual notation system with enforced invariants. Four-state classification (NORMATIVE / NON-NORMATIVE / CRITICAL / METACOGNITIVE) realised as the Klein four-group V4, encoded redundantly through color, orientation, and textual label. v3.0.1 is a PATCH-level errata and toolchain release on top of v3.0.0. It inserts one clarifying sentence into System section 4A.1 defining the locus-of-audit axis's frame pole (the premises, method, or evaluative assumptions under which a claim is judged — one's own frame, audited at METACOGNITIVE, or the framework the claim rests on, inverted at CRITICAL), so the specification and the inter-rater-reliability study instruments define the axis identically. It also switches PDF generation to the parity-proven owl-semaphore-press package (a byte-identical Typst-source parity test proves the extracted design language faithful to the legacy generator) and folds in repository-side additions (IRR pilot study toolkit, governance documentation) and post-publication documentation corrections accumulated since the v3.0.0 tag. The V4 algebra, the four state-operator tuples, the sigma_h assignment to METACOGNITIVE, the canonical formal sentence, the triple-redundant accessibility rule, the color/orientation semantics, and the asset set are unchanged from v3.0.0."
keywords:
